    "node-1plwz9r": {
      "supported": false,
      "issue": "The node claims 'Standard pre-maintenance steps were followed' but cites a source (24ec1587...) that only states the crew collected work folder and lock equipment. The detail asserts an absence of verified system configuration check contributed to vulnerability; however, no evidence confirms whether such checks are required by procedure or if they were omitted.",
      "evidenceNeeded": "A record establishing the specific pre-maintenance checklist requirements for WO-527 (including valve status confirmation) and a field observation log confirming whether those steps were performed at 09:35–09:48.",
      "question": "Does procedure ECP-1SC-04 Revision 3 require verification of system configuration (e.g., valve positions) before starting work on WO-527? If yes, is there a field record confirming this was done or omitted at the time?"
    },
    "node-1ssx536": {
      "supported": false,
      "issue": "The node asserts 'Maintenance receiver M-A had boundary acceptance pending' based on source b678a928...#1 which states that a scheduled work order does not mean the boundary is released. However, no evidence confirms whether formal release was actually pending at shift start or if it occurred later; this remains an inference without direct record of signature status.",
      "evidenceNeeded": "The signed copy (or timestamped log) of ECP-1SC-04 Revision 3 showing the maintenance acceptance field state at shift start time, and any associated communication confirming pending release.",
      "question": "Is there a dated electronic or physical record indicating that the boundary for WO-527 was not formally released by RHOB operations before 10:00 AM on May 20?"
    },
    "node-1okpyu9": {
      "supported": true,
      "issue": "",
