      "question": ""
    }
  },"decision":{
"summary":"Two of three proposed nodes lack full evidentiary support. Node node-1plwz9r assumes procedural compliance and omission without confirming requirements or execution records; it requires a procedure definition and field log for verification. Node node-1ssx536 infers pending acceptance from general policy rather than specific signature evidence at the relevant time. Only node-1okpyu9 is fully supported by point register mapping showing AL-44 maps to pressure, not compressor trip.",
"evidenceUsed":["b678a928-a8d2-472d-bc03-2e1a3dc411e6#1","da0260c0-7d49-43e8-b074-da2a14c7d59c#1","incident-description"],"unknowns":["Whether valve status checks were required or performed for WO-527.","Exact timestamp of boundary release signature on ECP-1SC-04 Revision 3."],"alternatives":["The pressure drop may have been caused upstream without any procedural violation if valves remained closed as intended.", "Boundary acceptance could have occurred after shift start but before the incident, making 'pending' status inaccurate at event time."],"confidence":0.72}
